  "note": "Digests of pooled, hidden, outputs, fastOut and rewardTrace (docs/designs/wasm-kernels.md; test/sim/helpers/brain-reference.js), written by scripts/record-brain-reference.mjs. First recorded from the JS forwardAll before wasm-kernels T7 deleted it, and since re-recorded from the Rust kernel when a change moved what a case does (realistic-keepers T22, the rewardedHebb deletion, body-genes T7 for the pooled-v6 row sizes). Re-recorded at body-genes T31, when pool started carrying the size, speed and closing lanes of the prey and threat hits and writing the four view shares, and the per-call cases started filling those lanes; the naive pooling reference of test/sim/ray-pool.test.js (extended with the body sense) agrees with the kernel. The independent multi-tick reference of wasm-kernels.md T33 is not built yet. Stepped digests re-recorded when a startled herd stopped holding its centroid (role-budget T21a, `summarizeGroup`); the per-call cases are unchanged. Stepped digests re-recorded for smoke dropped toward a hunter in front (feat(sim)!: smokeAimArc): a world where a releaser has a hunter ahead drops its cloud elsewhere. Stepped digests re-recorded again when the smoke aim moved from a scan of every agent to the nearest threat on the releaser's own rays (perf/smoke-aim-local-sensing): a releaser aims along a ray, not at the hunter's bearing. Stepped digests re-recorded for the smoke decoy (feat(sim)!: smokeDecoyTicks): a fresh cloud also reads on the prey channel, so a hunter whose rays meet a cloud sees a body in it. Stepped digests re-recorded for the step 5 adoption (feat(sim)!: step5-e as the defaults): every stepped world steps differently; the per-call digests are unchanged.",
